RECEIVED POWER LEVEL ANALYSIS
If the transmitter’s effective radiated power (ERP) is specified in the transmitter’s .lrp file, or expressed on
the command-line using the -erp switch, and the -dbm switch is invoked, received power level contours ref-
erenced to decibels over one milliwatt (dBm) are produced:
.IP
.B splat -t wnjt-dt -L 30.0 -erp 46000 -dbm -db -100 -o plot.ppm
.PP 
The -db switch can be used to limit the extent to which received power level contours are plotted. When
plotting power level contours, the argument given is interpreted as being expressed in dBm.
\fBSPLAT!\fR received power level color definition files share a very similar structure to the color definition files
described earlier, except that the power levels in dBm may be either positive or neg ative, and are limited to
